WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.920 --> 00:00:04.680
-Isabel Eriksson, welcome.
-Thank you.

00:00:07.720 --> 00:00:14.520
This story starts when you meet a man
for the second time in your apartment.

00:00:14.680 --> 00:00:18.920
What did you know about this man?

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:31.800
He said he lived in London
and worked within finance.

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:31.800
He said he lived in London
and worked within finance.

00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:35.240
He was well built.

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:41.360
He was a little bit shorter than me.

00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:45.960
He seemed calm and collected.

00:00:46.120 --> 00:00:49.480
He seemed intelligent.

00:00:49.640 --> 00:00:54.200
He had brought with him-

00:00:54.360 --> 00:01:01.280
-strawberries dipped in chocolate
and champagne.

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:06.720
He had laced the berries
with a sleeping agent.

00:01:06.880 --> 00:01:12.480
What do you remember from that night?

00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:23.280
I remember that he wanted
to feed me strawberries.

00:01:25.760 --> 00:01:29.400
It's hard to talk about.

00:01:29.560 --> 00:01:35.560
I fell asleep soon after,
and everything went black.

00:01:35.720 --> 00:01:41.840
-He then put you in his car.
-Yes.

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:49.000
He took you to southern Sweden.
What did you see when you woke up?

00:01:50.080 --> 00:01:53.400
I saw a tin roof-

00:01:53.560 --> 00:01:58.960
-and a man sitting on a chair next to me.

00:01:59.120 --> 00:02:01.600
He was just looking at me.

00:02:02.800 --> 00:02:09.280
I had a needle in my arm. I ripped it out.

00:02:09.440 --> 00:02:15.400
He said he had kidnapped me and wanted
to keep me for a couple of years.

00:02:15.560 --> 00:02:20.200
A couple of years?
So he told you what his plans were?

00:02:20.360 --> 00:02:23.680
-Yes.
-You had quite a strong reaction.

00:02:23.840 --> 00:02:29.480
Yes, I tried to attack him and escape.

00:02:29.640 --> 00:02:33.400
I attacked him with two nails.

00:02:33.560 --> 00:02:38.880
But I was still drugged,
so it didn't go well.

00:02:39.040 --> 00:02:42.720
He grabbed my wrists-

00:02:42.880 --> 00:02:47.320
-and said that if I tried that again,
he would chain me to the bed-

00:02:47.480 --> 00:02:51.040
-and only feed me crispbread.

00:02:51.200 --> 00:02:55.280
How did you feel? You didn't know if you
were above or below the ground.

00:02:55.440 --> 00:02:59.680
It was an unfinished room-

00:02:59.840 --> 00:03:03.760
-with a lot of dust.

00:03:05.320 --> 00:03:08.400
It was cold, dusty,

00:03:08.560 --> 00:03:12.560
with stone floors
and bags of cement everywhere.

00:03:12.720 --> 00:03:16.760
He told me he built it all himself.

00:03:16.920 --> 00:03:21.200
He told me in detail how he had built it.

00:03:21.360 --> 00:03:25.440
He seemed very proud of it.

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:31.840
-There were three vault doors.
-Yes.

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:35.280
Two of them had an electronic code lock.

00:03:35.440 --> 00:03:39.800
Did he ever let you out-

00:03:39.960 --> 00:03:42.720
-so you could get some fresh air?

00:03:42.880 --> 00:03:49.360
Yes, he let me out sometimes.
He had built a little exercise yard...

00:03:50.720 --> 00:03:53.400
Outside the bunker.

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:57.200
Can you see where you are?

00:03:57.360 --> 00:04:03.640
No. I can only see trees.
So I have no idea where I am.

00:04:05.520 --> 00:04:12.080
He took you dog with him. A small dog.

00:04:12.240 --> 00:04:16.120
How did he treat it?

00:04:16.280 --> 00:04:21.640
He took her for walks every morning.

00:04:21.800 --> 00:04:27.400
One day he came in
with a black plastic box-

00:04:27.560 --> 00:04:33.840
-and said that she would have to
do her business in the box.

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:36.120
If not, he would get rid of her.

00:04:38.400 --> 00:04:42.880
-The dog was important to you.
-Yes, very.

00:04:44.160 --> 00:04:49.920
One day he came in with a mask on.
He had bought some masks.

00:04:50.080 --> 00:04:55.480
His plan was to wear it
during the abduction.

00:04:55.640 --> 00:04:59.920
Was that to scare you?
I don't understand.

00:05:00.080 --> 00:05:05.880
-One day he came in...
-An authentic looking mask.

00:05:06.040 --> 00:05:09.440
Yes, it looked very genuine.

00:05:09.600 --> 00:05:15.320
It didn't look like him.
I didn't know who entered the room.

00:05:17.080 --> 00:05:21.240
I told him I had been kidnapped
and that I was being held captive.

00:05:21.400 --> 00:05:25.160
I was hoping this person could help me.

00:05:25.320 --> 00:05:30.160
But then he removed the mask-

00:05:30.320 --> 00:05:35.360
-and I saw that it was him.

00:05:36.360 --> 00:05:41.360
He said I looked very surprised.

00:05:41.520 --> 00:05:46.640
-Did he find it funny?
-Yes, it was some kind of joke.

00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:51.800
Did he have mood swings?

00:05:51.960 --> 00:05:57.400
Yes. He was very calm-

00:05:57.560 --> 00:06:01.040
-and intimidating at the same time.

00:06:01.200 --> 00:06:05.720
He came in with a gun on the Monday.

00:06:05.880 --> 00:06:09.280
He wanted me to shoot him.

00:06:09.440 --> 00:06:11.480
-He wanted you to shoot him?
-Yes.

00:06:11.640 --> 00:06:15.520
He gave me the gun
and told me that the doors were open-

00:06:15.680 --> 00:06:20.040
-and I could just shoot him and leave.

00:06:20.200 --> 00:06:25.000
But I couldn't shoot anyone.

00:06:25.160 --> 00:06:29.960
And I didn't know if the doors
were really open.

00:06:31.800 --> 00:06:36.120
On Friday he came back with the gun-

00:06:36.280 --> 00:06:40.040
-and told me he wanted me to shoot him.

00:06:40.200 --> 00:06:46.800
Did he tell you why he wanted you
to shoot him? Is he depressed?

00:06:46.960 --> 00:06:53.640
He told me he could never
survive in prison.

00:06:53.800 --> 00:06:57.360
So he wanted me to shoot him.

00:06:59.760 --> 00:07:03.160
But it wasn't a real gun.

00:07:03.320 --> 00:07:09.480
He wanted to test my intentions.

00:07:10.800 --> 00:07:14.880
So I'm glad I never pulled the trigger.

00:07:17.080 --> 00:07:23.280
You realized
that the place was escape proof.

00:07:23.440 --> 00:07:27.840
Only he knew the codes.
So you were dependent on him.

00:07:28.000 --> 00:07:32.320
If anything were to happen to him,
you'd never get out.

00:07:32.480 --> 00:07:35.080
That's right.

00:07:35.240 --> 00:07:39.960
What was your survival strategy?

00:07:40.120 --> 00:07:44.160
I tried to escape when I first arrived.

00:07:44.320 --> 00:07:49.840
But I realized I wouldn't
be able to overpower him.

00:07:50.000 --> 00:07:56.160
The bunker was escape proof,
so I couldn't get out.

00:07:57.920 --> 00:08:02.280
So I had to start playing my cards right.

00:08:02.440 --> 00:08:05.400
I didn't want him to see me as a threat.

00:08:05.560 --> 00:08:11.080
So I chose to be courteous and neutral.

00:08:12.520 --> 00:08:18.560
I thought that might make him trust me-

00:08:18.720 --> 00:08:23.040
-so that I could find
an opportunity to escape.

00:08:24.400 --> 00:08:29.200
You're here today,
so it must have been a good strategy.

00:08:29.360 --> 00:08:34.520
I don't believe you had sex in the bunker.

00:08:34.680 --> 00:08:41.520
But he stayed with you one night.
Can you tell us about that?

00:08:43.640 --> 00:08:48.000
Yes, he wanted us to sleep together.

00:08:51.760 --> 00:08:57.440
It was horrible to sleep next to
someone who had kidnapped you.

00:08:57.600 --> 00:09:01.120
He wanted body contact all night.

00:09:03.440 --> 00:09:09.400
He has a plan.
He wants you to be his girlfriend.

00:09:09.560 --> 00:09:15.000
But he doesn't initiate sex.

00:09:15.160 --> 00:09:19.520
Do you have any idea why?

00:09:19.680 --> 00:09:25.240
Yes, he took some tests.
Blood tests and such.

00:09:27.120 --> 00:09:30.960
He wanted to make sure
I didn't have any diseases.

00:09:31.120 --> 00:09:34.360
Because he wanted to have
unprotected sex.

00:09:34.520 --> 00:09:40.240
When we slept together that Wednesday,

00:09:40.400 --> 00:09:45.720
he didn't want to have sex
until the test results were back.

00:09:45.880 --> 00:09:49.200
What did he do when he wasn't with you?

00:09:49.360 --> 00:09:53.680
Did he work?
Did he have a normal life as a doctor?

00:09:53.840 --> 00:09:57.200
Yes, he was working as a doctor.

00:10:01.440 --> 00:10:04.320
His plan is for this to be long term.

00:10:04.480 --> 00:10:09.880
-He also plans to kidnap more women.
-Yes.

00:10:10.040 --> 00:10:13.480
But he couldn't do it.

00:10:13.640 --> 00:10:17.280
And one day he tells you
that you're free to go.

00:10:18.520 --> 00:10:23.760
Did he tell you why he couldn't do it?

00:10:25.120 --> 00:10:30.000
Yes, on the Friday
he went back to Stockholm.

00:10:30.160 --> 00:10:34.800
He was picking up my belongings
from my apartment.

00:10:34.960 --> 00:10:41.880
He found a note on my door
which said I was missing-

00:10:42.040 --> 00:10:47.760
-and that the police
had changed the locks, so he can't get in.

00:10:49.480 --> 00:10:53.080
So he came back to the bunker-

00:10:53.240 --> 00:10:58.320
-and told me to tell them I was with him
of my own free will-

00:10:58.480 --> 00:11:00.760
-and that we would make up a story.

00:11:00.920 --> 00:11:06.400
That he hadn't kidnapped me, but that
I was with him of my own free will.

00:11:06.560 --> 00:11:11.440
So he wanted you to come with him
to the police to get your keys?

00:11:11.600 --> 00:11:17.920
Yes, and to prove
that I hadn't been kidnapped.

00:11:20.920 --> 00:11:24.880
How was the drive to Stockholm?

00:11:25.040 --> 00:11:28.200
I tried to stay calm.

00:11:29.480 --> 00:11:33.120
I had no idea what he was going to do.

00:11:33.280 --> 00:11:39.040
If he was going to show the police
I was fine-

00:11:39.200 --> 00:11:42.520
-and then kidnap me again.

00:11:42.680 --> 00:11:47.560
I was terrified the entire time
and didn't know what he was going to do.

00:11:47.720 --> 00:11:53.040
-Did you have a conversation?
-Yes.

00:11:53.200 --> 00:11:56.520
What did he want to talk about?

00:11:56.680 --> 00:12:00.240
Anything and everything.

00:12:00.400 --> 00:12:05.680
He told me he didn't expect me
to be as nice as I was.

00:12:05.840 --> 00:12:10.920
He said that if I hadn't been so nice,
he wouldn't have let me out.

00:12:11.080 --> 00:12:15.480
Then I would have deserved
to stay in there.

00:12:16.280 --> 00:12:19.480
-He came with you to the police station.
-Yes.

00:12:19.640 --> 00:12:25.000
You had to wait for two hours.
It was an absurd situation.

00:12:25.160 --> 00:12:26.760
Yes, it was.

00:12:26.920 --> 00:12:31.880
-Did you feel free?
-No.

00:12:33.280 --> 00:12:35.600
When did you feel free?

00:12:35.760 --> 00:12:40.880
When I came into a room
to talk to an investigator.

00:12:41.040 --> 00:12:44.880
-And he wasn't allowed in?
-No.

00:12:45.040 --> 00:12:50.440
That's when I broke down-

00:12:50.600 --> 00:12:54.640
-and told them that I had been kidnapped-

00:12:54.800 --> 00:12:57.640
-and that the kidnapper
was sitting right there.

00:12:57.800 --> 00:12:59.360
That's when they arrested him.

00:12:59.520 --> 00:13:03.680
-He was arrested and later convicted.
-Yes.

00:13:06.000 --> 00:13:11.280
You met this doctor because
you were working as an escort.

00:13:11.440 --> 00:13:15.560
-And he was a client.
-Yes.

00:13:17.480 --> 00:13:19.120
-You don't do that anymore.
-No.

00:13:19.280 --> 00:13:24.080
-Would you be able to do that job again?
-No, absolutely not.

00:13:24.240 --> 00:13:30.760
When I was working as an escort,
I had to lead a double life.

00:13:32.280 --> 00:13:36.400
It was difficult
to have serious relationships.

00:13:36.560 --> 00:13:43.080
Since the kidnapping I see life
differently and have different values.

00:13:43.240 --> 00:13:46.320
What kind of help have you received?

00:13:46.480 --> 00:13:50.560
I'm still in therapy to process
what happened to me.

00:13:52.480 --> 00:13:55.480
Has it changed you as a person,

00:13:55.640 --> 00:14:00.160
compared to what you were like
before this happened?

00:14:00.320 --> 00:14:04.720
Yes, I've changed a lot.

00:14:06.400 --> 00:14:12.120
I stopped working
as an escort immediately.

00:14:12.280 --> 00:14:16.720
I realized what's important in life.

00:14:16.880 --> 00:14:23.040
Before this happened,
easy money and travel-

00:14:23.200 --> 00:14:27.160
-were important to me.

00:14:27.320 --> 00:14:30.600
But now I have
completely different values.

00:14:30.760 --> 00:14:35.280
I used to be
very fearless and adventurous.

00:14:35.440 --> 00:14:41.440
But now I'm more scared and cautious.

00:14:43.240 --> 00:14:47.200
You're a more cautious person.
What are your plans for the future?

00:14:49.080 --> 00:14:53.960
I want to study. Maybe abroad.

00:14:56.200 --> 00:15:02.320
Right now I'm focusing on taking it
one day at a time and get my life back.

00:15:04.440 --> 00:15:10.680
The doctor will be released one day.
What are your thoughts on that?

00:15:11.520 --> 00:15:15.520
I'm very scared.

00:15:17.360 --> 00:15:21.760
It's terrifying knowing
that he will be released soon.

00:15:21.920 --> 00:15:27.640
I'm under witness protection,
and will continue to be for a while.

00:15:29.480 --> 00:15:34.040
Thank you very much
for telling us your story.

00:15:39.880 --> 00:15:44.840
Your book is called
"I bunkerläkarens våld".

00:15:45.000 --> 00:15:48.840
It's out now.
Thank you very much for coming.

